s have high unseen (4 each), but there are many different ones, so keeping all might be inefficient. I could discard one terminal that seems safe. W9 was just discarded, so it's safe. Also, discarding W9 might signal that I don't need W9, which is true.  \n\nAlternatively, T9 is a terminal, but not recently discarded. T1 not recently discarded. B1 not recently discarded. So W9 is the safest among terminals.  \n\nI'll go with W9.  \n\nReason: W9 is a terminal tile that was just discarded by the next player, making it a relatively safe discard to avoid giving other players what they need. My hand is scattered with many singles, and I have a triplet of B2, so I should aim for a pung-based hand like All Pungs combined with Dragon Pung to reach the 8-point threshold. Discarding W9, which is isolated and not part of any promising sequence or potential pung (since I only have one), helps streamline my hand toward collecting pairs and pungs of other tiles like J2 or remaining terminals. Keeping the B2 triplet is essential, and I should retain honors and other terminals that might contribute to scoring patterns.\n\nAnswer: Play W9"}
